Environmental Standards and Global Mining Expectations
Mining companies operate under a combination of national regulations, environmental permits, industry standards and stakeholder expectations.

Several international frameworks can help guide environmental management practices.

ISO 14001 – Environmental Management Systems: Provides a framework for establishing, implementing, maintaining and improving an environmental management system.

ISO 45001 – Occupational Health and Safety Management Systems: Supports systematic management of workplace health and safety risks.

Global Industry Standard on Tailings Management (GISTM): Establishes expectations for responsible tailings facility management, including governance, affected communities and risk management.

GHG Protocol: Provides widely used standards and guidance for greenhouse gas accounting and reporting.

International Council on Mining and Metals (ICMM): Publishes industry principles and resources relating to responsible mining practices.

Digital EHS software can help organize information and workflows associated with these frameworks, but using software does not itself establish certification or conformity.

