Frequently Asked Questions
What is mining environmental management software?

Mining environmental management software is a digital platform used to organize environmental monitoring, compliance obligations, inspections, incidents, risk assessments and corrective actions associated with mining operations.

How does digital EHS improve environmental compliance in mining?

Digital EHS can improve the management of compliance obligations through centralized records, assigned responsibilities, scheduled activities, documented evidence and corrective-action tracking. It does not guarantee regulatory compliance.

Can AI help prevent environmental incidents in mines?

AI can help identify unusual trends and recurring environmental risks, supporting earlier investigation and preventive action. Its effectiveness depends on reliable data and appropriate human review.

Can NeoEHS support water and air-quality management?

NeoEHS includes environmental and air-quality management capabilities. Water-monitoring workflows and specific equipment integrations should be confirmed against the proposed deployment scope.

How does EHS software support sustainable mining?

It helps organizations manage environmental information, identify recurring issues, coordinate corrective actions and track selected sustainability indicators.

Can mining companies use one EHS platform across multiple sites?

Yes. A centralized EHS platform can support standardized workflows across locations while allowing configuration for site-specific environmental requirements.

Does digital EHS replace ISO 14001?

No. ISO 14001 is an environmental management system standard. Digital EHS software can support implementation and record management, but it does not replace the standard or independent certification processes.
